    {
      "id": "HOM-02",
      "title": "Degree shift for a group acting on an exact face complex",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-degree-two-stabilizers",
      "statement": "For an exact augmented permutation face complex through degree m, with at most A orbits and stabilizers of order ≤s in degrees through m, |tors H_m(G,ℤ)|≤(m+2)^A s^(mA s^m). At GL_N(O_L) this yields the homological ingredient of K_24 and the later witness 141 for the locally trivial group.",
      "hypotheses": "Group action with equivariant faces and exact augmented chain complex (surjective augmentation). s≥1. For the number-field application L totally complex, n=[L:ℚ], e≥1, 1≤N≤4e+6 and m≤2e+1. The geometric orbit-count and stabilizer theorems are separate inputs.",
